Currently, the specification states [these|http://docs.jboss.org/cdi/spec/2.0/cdi-spec.html#what_classes_are_beans ] limitations on what classes are beans. Namely it mentions that:

_It has an appropriate constructor - either_
_* the class has a constructor with no parameters, or_
_* the class declares a constructor annotated @Inject._

This effectively means that a class which has single constructor that is parameterized and does not have {{@Inject}} annotation on it will not become a bean. In fact, it will blow the CDI up. Just like this class:

{code}
@ApplicationScoped
public class Foo {
  // no @Inject annotation and no other constructor present
  public Foo(Bar bar) {
  }
}
{code}

Could we loosen the limitation and in the above case automatically _assume_ (effectively add) the {{@Inject}} annotation?

